DESCRIPTION:At 79 years old\, New Jersey Senator Loretta Weinberg wasn’t s
 lowing down—she was at the height of her influence and just getting start
 ed.\nAffectionately known as the “Feisty Grandma\,” the former Senate maj
 ority leader built a reputation for challenging powerful figures\, standi
 ng up for what she believed in\, and refusing to stay quiet. She turned N
 ew Jersey politics upside down when she helped uncover the infamous Bridg
 egate scandal\, contributing to Governor Chris Christie’s dramatic fall f
 rom power and proving that determination can shake even the strongest pol
 itical establishment.\nBut behind the headlines\, heated debates\, and po
 litical victories is a warm and wonderfully complicated mother-daughter s
 tory. Told through that personal lens\, Politics Is a Mother: Raising Hel
 l Is Part of the Job offers a funny\, heartfelt\, and revealing look at t
 he woman behind the public figure. It explores how family shaped Weinberg
 ’s political life—and how politics became part of the family.\nFull of hu
 mor\, heart\, history\, and a healthy dose of hell-raising\, this story s
 hows why the political is always personal. It also proves that an “adorab
 le grandmother” can be a fearless advocate\, a relentless reformer\, and 
 one of the most important and influential politicians of our time.\n\nHos
 ted by: Civic & Voter Engagement\, Government Relations and Community Aff
 airs \n\nAdditional Information can be found at: https://montclair.campus
 labs.com/engage/event/12651811
DTEND:20260929T003000Z
DTSTAMP:20260926T045349Z
DTSTART:20260928T213000Z
LOCATION:College of Coms and Media: Presentation Hall
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Movie Screening of Politics is a Mother: Raising Hell is Part of t
 he Job
UID:https://montclair.campuslabs.com/engage/event/12651811
URL:https://montclair.campuslabs.com/engage/event/12651811
X-HOSTS:Government Relations and Community Affairs
