BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Montclair State University
CATEGORIES:ThoughtfulLearning
CATEGORIES:Academic/Educational/Intellectual
DESCRIPTION:Please complete this RSVP form to confirm your registration! S
 chool of Communication and Media\, Presentation Hall Wednesday\, Oct. 7 a
 t 6:00pm\nThe Coccia Institute at Montclair State University welcomes New
  York Times Rome bureau correspondent Jason Horowitz to discuss The Itali
 an Job with Coccia director Mark Rotella.\n \nFrom Venetian canals to Vat
 ican conclaves\, New York Times correspondent Jason Horowitz takes you on
  a tour of the real Italy.\n \nItaly’s deep history\, stunning landscapes
  and glorious food have uniquely captured our imagination. In The Italian
  Job\, Jason Horowitz\, a longtime Rome bureau chief for The New York Tim
 es\, tells the story of how he too fell under that Tuscan-sun enchantment
 \, before ultimately discovering a more fascinating Italy\, a country con
 ducting experiments in populist politics\, confronting global challenges 
 like immigration\, climate change and an aging population.\n \nHorowitz i
 ntroduces us to an extraordinary range of characters. He flies with popes
  and drinks Spritzes with prime ministers\, talks beauty with top fashion
  designers in Milan\, ponders the big questions with cardinals in Rome\, 
 and gets his feet wet in the Venice lagoon with engineers trying to save 
 the sinking city. Throughout\, Italy’s streets\, layered with history\, a
 nd its cafés\, vibrating with conversation\, are full of lessons. So is h
 is life at home\, where his Italian wife and their two children offer an 
 even more intimate\, concentrated and rollicking view of Italian life. As
  years pass and the world turns upside down\, Italy\, more than a vacatio
 n destination or land of the past\, reveals itself as a vivid lens throug
 h which to understand our present and future.\n\nHosted by: College of Hu
 manities and Social Sciences (CHSS)\n\nAdditional Information can be foun
 d at: https://montclair.campuslabs.com/engage/event/12812653
DTEND:20261008T000000Z
DTSTAMP:20260926T045349Z
DTSTART:20261007T220000Z
GEO:40.859750;-74.199750
LOCATION:School of Communication and Media\, Presentation Hall
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:The Italian Job: Jason Horowitz in conversation with Mark Rotella
UID:https://montclair.campuslabs.com/engage/event/12812653
URL:https://montclair.campuslabs.com/engage/event/12812653
X-HOSTS:College of Humanities and Social Sciences (CHSS)
