BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Montclair State University
CATEGORIES:ThoughtfulLearning
DESCRIPTION:Drawing inspiration from the mid-1960s anti-war movement\, thi
 s teach-in will be an action-based educational forum concerning modern US
  foreign interventionism and its historical convergence with Iran during 
 the Cold War. More specifically\, it will focus on the rise of the postwa
 r national security state and its first pivotal and consequential “win”: 
 the 1953 Iranian coup d'état. It was the first "successful" overthrow of 
 a democratically elected foreign leader by the CIA (and definitely not th
 e last). It is a tale that is regularly expunged from conventional Americ
 an history\, yet it is vastly significant to both Iranian US history. Thi
 s chapter elucidates\, in part\, why both nations find themselves where t
 hey are today. In addition\, this teach-in will also highlight the determ
 ining role of big business\, military keynesianism\, and neocolonialism i
 n shaping the confines of postwar U.S. foreign policy. This teach-in will
  conclude with a discussion on what this all means for the ongoing US-Isr
 aeli war against Iran\, and what actionable acts can be done to end the c
 onflict.\n\nHosted by: The Apple Core Community\n\nAdditional Information
  can be found at: https://montclair.campuslabs.com/engage/event/12686214
DTEND:20261015T230000Z
DTSTAMP:20260926T045349Z
DTSTART:20261015T203000Z
LOCATION:Student Center 250A - Ballroom A
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:ACC Teach-In: On the Origins of Modern US Foreign Interventionism 
 & Iran
UID:https://montclair.campuslabs.com/engage/event/12686214
URL:https://montclair.campuslabs.com/engage/event/12686214
X-HOSTS:The Apple Core Community
END:VEVENT
